    "productVersion": "1.0.0-beta.2",
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-05 02:16:09",
    "releaseNotes": "# AID v1.0.0-beta.2\n\n## 中文说明\n\n这是 AID 的第二个公开 Beta 测试版本。本次同版本强制重发同步更新服务端、后台管理端、Web 用户端、开源初始化 SQL 与升级器，重点完善源码构建式部署、供应链校验、配置管理和在线升级的可靠性。\n\n### 本次更新\n\n- 一键部署与升级继续采用三端同名 Tag 源码构建，不下载主程序大包；版本清单、三端源码与升级器均优先使用 Gitee，Gitee 不可用时整组切换到 GitHub，避免三个仓库混用不同来源。\n- 新增依赖区域策略 `auto / cn / global`。Maven、npm、Go、JDK、Node 与 Maven 下载均支持主源失败后切换备用源，后台升级配置页可统一管理该策略。\n- 固定构建工具链为 JDK 17.0.20、Node.js 22.22.0、Maven 3.9.9 和 Go 1.22.12，并对下载内容执行官方校验值验证，减少不同服务器环境导致的构建差异。\n- Docker 官方基础镜像使用不可变摘要；国内镜像拉取后核对官方摘要，校验不一致时拒绝继续，防止标签漂移或镜像内容被替换。\n- 升级时同步刷新受版本控制的部署脚本与 Docker Compose 文件，同时保留用户的 `.env` 和运行配置；仅重建 AID 应用容器，不主动重建 MySQL、Redis、RocketMQ 或升级器容器。\n- Docker 与 systemd 部署继续坚持“先配置、确认后部署”。配置文件升级采用同目录备份和缺项补齐，既有配置值不覆盖；应用后自动重启并执行健康检查。\n- 首次初始化不再使用固定后台访问码。安装器会生成 12 位强随机访问码，已有非空访问码保持不变；后台管理端也只使用安全随机源生成访问码。\n- 外部或内置 MySQL、Redis、RocketMQ、HTTPS 证书与端口配置继续统一由部署配置管理；外部服务启用后不启动对应内置服务。\n- 修复分镜图片、视频生成链路中的任务续接、结果回填和错误归一化处理，并补充自动化回归测试。\n- Web 端完善视频预览交互与分集时间轴映射，新增时间轴映射测试；后台管理端补充依赖区域配置和访问码安全校验。\n- 更新 `sql/aid-init.sql` 与 `sql/v1.0.0-beta.2.sql`，用于全新安装和已有 Beta 环境的幂等升级。\n- Gitee Release 作为主下载源、GitHub Release 作为备用下载源，两端均只交付 Linux amd64/arm64 两个小型升级器，不上传主程序包、官方资产包或 `checksums.txt`。\n\n### 测试版提示\n\n本版本仍为 Beta 测试版。生产环境升级前请备份数据库、配置文件、上传目录和对象存储数据，并尽量在没有生成任务运行时执行升级。部署完成后请妥善保存安装器输出的后台访问路径，并立即修改默认管理员密码。\n\n## English Notes\n\nThis is the second public beta release of AID. This replacement release synchronizes the server, administration console, Web client, open-source SQL, and updater, with a focus on reproducible source builds, supply-chain verification, configuration safety, and reliable online upgrades.\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Installation and upgrades continue to build matching tags from all three repositories instead of downloading a large application archive. Manifests, source tags, and updater packages use Gitee first and switch all repositories to GitHub together only when Gitee is unavailable.\n- Added the `auto / cn / global` dependency-region policy. Maven, npm, Go, JDK, Node.js, and Maven downloads can retry through an alternate source, and the policy is configurable from the administration upgrade page.\n- Pinned the build toolchain to JDK 17.0.20, Node.js 22.22.0, Maven 3.9.9, and Go 1.22.12, with official checksum verification for downloaded toolchains.\n- Official Docker base images are pinned by immutable digest. Images fetched through the domestic mirror must match the official digest before they are accepted.\n- Upgrades now refresh version-controlled deployment scripts and Docker Compose assets while preserving the user's `.env` and runtime configuration. Only AID application containers are recreated; MySQL, Redis, RocketMQ, and the updater are left untouched.\n- Docker and systemd deployments remain configuration-first. Configuration upgrades create a same-directory backup and add only missing keys without overwriting existing values, followed by restart and health verification.\n- Fresh installations no longer use a fixed administration access code. The installer generates a cryptographically strong 12-character code, while existing non-empty codes remain unchanged.\n- External and embedded MySQL, Redis, RocketMQ, HTTPS certificate, and port settings remain centrally managed. Embedded services are not started when external services are configured.\n- Improved storyboard image/video task continuation, result write-back, and normalized error handling, with additional regression tests.\n- Improved Web video-preview behavior and episode timeline mapping, and added administration controls for dependency regions and secure access-code validation.\n- Refreshed `sql/aid-init.sql` and `sql/v1.0.0-beta.2.sql` for clean installations and idempotent upgrades from existing beta deployments.\n- Gitee Release is the primary download source and GitHub Release is the fallback. Both contain only the small Linux amd64/arm64 updater archives; no application archive, official asset bundle, or `checksums.txt` is published.\n\n### Beta Notice\n\nThis remains a beta release. Back up the database, configuration files, upload directory, and object-storage data before upgrading a production environment, and avoid upgrading while generation tasks are active. Keep the generated administration URL secure and change the default administrator password immediately after deployment.",
